quran[4]{c,v,t}:
  2,216,"Fighting (in defence) has (now) been prescribed for you, though it is an object of dislike to you. However, you may hate a thing while it is good for you, and you may love a thing while it is bad for you. Allah knows, and you do not know."
  2,217,"(O Prophet!) They ask you about fighting in the sacred month. Say fighting in it is a grave offence, but hindering (others) from the path of Allah, disbelieving in Him, preventing (the worshippers from access to) the Holy Mosque and expelling its people from it are far greater (offences) in the sight of Allah. And persecution is worse than killing. And they will not cease fighting you until they turn you away from your religion if they can. But whoever from you turns away from his religion and dies as a disbeliever—they are the ones whose (previous) works (of devotion) shall come to nothing in this world and the Hereafter. They shall be the inhabitants of the Fire, remaining in it forever."
  2,218,"Those who have believed and those who have migrated (because of persecution) and have striven hard for Allah’s cause, it is they who shall expect Allah’s Mercy, and Allah is Most Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  2,219,"They ask you about drinking (wine) and gambling. Say: ‘There is a great sin in both, although they have some means of profit for the people, and their sin is far greater than their profit.’ And they (also) ask you what they should spend. Say: ‘All that is surplus’. Thus, Allah clarifies His revelations to you, so perhaps you may reflect,"
